    title_en: "WhatsApp for Android Vulnerability Allows Viewing Private Photos on Unlocked Devices",
    summary_en: "Security researchers discovered a vulnerability in WhatsApp for Android that allows users to view private photos while the device is unlocked. The attack flow involves answering a WhatsApp call, and then when using the photo filter or AI editing features, the system previews the photo without requiring the user to enter a PIN or perform biometric authentication. However, this vulnerability is not universal; NotebookCheck found that Galaxy devices enforce unlocking, but Pixel and Oppo devices allow complete bypass. Notably, this vulnerability does not affect WhatsApp on iPhone because iOS mandates the use of the native calling interface. Currently, the vulnerability is limited to viewing photos and cannot bypass other parts of the device. WhatsApp has received the report and advises users to temporarily set WhatsApp's photo/video access permissions to 'Restricted' to mitigate this vulnerability.",
