    summary_en: "A survey conducted by Elon University and The Washington Post explored the trend of Americans viewing AI chatbots as virtual friends or psychological therapists. The results indicated that many people tend to form emotional connections with this type of entity. The article suggests that this finding strongly supports the decision that Apple must carefully design Siri AI to avoid encouraging the formation of false or excessive emotional relationships. This serves as a reminder to developers and tech companies that when integrating AI chat functions, they must consider not only technical stability but also the impact on user mental health and social psychology, preventing user psychological dependency or misunderstanding.",
