    title_en: "Nonprofit Organization Sues Federal Government: Demands Public Disclosure of AI Model Safety Review Framework",
    summary_en: "The nonpartisan nonprofit organization Protect Democracy has filed a lawsuit against multiple federal agencies, demanding public disclosure of the secret framework used by the government to conduct safety reviews of advanced AI models before release. The organization points out that the public and Congress have received almost no details, except for a few \"trusted partners.\" This lack of transparency affects the government's review process, the companies involved in building the framework, and the legal authority of federal officials conducting the reviews. The lawsuit demands that the government provide all information by September 30, including \"unclassified procedural and contractual architecture: the text of the framework, the terms of participation, the identity of participants, and the procedures and standards for granting or restricting access to advanced models.\" This action highlights the lack of oversight from Congress, the public, and external experts by the federal executive branch in deciding which AI models can be released, and which clients can access this technology, which could impact U.S. industry, national security, and even the global economy.",
