    title_en: "US Army Uses 20 kW High-Energy Laser System to Shoot Down Drones, Enhancing Border Defense Capabilities",
    summary_en: "The US Army recently conducted military exercises in the US-Mexico border region, successfully shooting down three drones using a High-Energy Multipurpose Laser (HEL) system. The operation was executed by the Joint Task Force Southern Border (JTF-SB) and aimed at countering targets perceived as posing a physical threat to US military and Customs and Border Protection (CBP) patrol units. The system technology originates from the Army's AMP-HEL project and was implemented using the Locust Laser Weapon System platform provided by defense technology company AeroVironment. The system can be mounted on military vehicles, operating at a power of 20 kW. It detects, tracks, and illuminates targets through a highly concentrated beam, combining this with sensors and radar technologies. The system can precisely focus the beam and convert additional electrical energy into heat, thereby damaging or disabling the target. This technology demonstrates the military's application and development of high-energy laser weapons in the field of border defense.",
