    title: "펜타시큐리티發布 D.AMO onOS v5.0，強化 Linux 環境非結構化數據及日誌加密保護",
    summary: "펜타시큐리티 發布了其非結構化數據加密產品 D.AMO onOS v5.0，旨在全面保護 Linux 環境中的非結構化數據，包括加密和解密日誌。該產品的重點在於縮小威脅暴露面，並在發生洩露事件時從源頭上阻止損害。鑑於近期個人資訊洩露事件常發生在未加密日誌、長期閒置數據或金鑰管理疏忽等安全盲區，數據中心安全策略變得至關重要。D.AMO onOS v5.0 可加密包括閒置數據在內的所有數據，從而消除攻擊者可利用的弱點。此外，它還加密所有日誌數據，包括解密記錄，確保即使數據洩露，攻擊者也無法獲取明文。該產品在 NFS 或 Samba 等大型網路文件系統環境中，確保了接近明文環境的加密性能，並提高了系統的可用性。該平台已整合 NIST 標準量子抗性加密 (PQC) 和韓國型量子抗性加密 (KpqC) 演算法，為量子計算時代做好了準備。",
    tags: ["펜타시큐리티", "D.AMO onOS v5.0", "數據加密", "Linux", "PQC", "數據安全"],
    title_en: "PentaSecurity Releases D.AMO onOS v5.0 to Enhance Encryption Protection for Unstructured Data and Logs in Linux Environments",
    summary_en: "PentaSecurity has released D.AMO onOS v5.0, its unstructured data encryption product, designed to comprehensively protect unstructured data in Linux environments, including encrypted and decrypted logs. The product focuses on reducing the threat surface and preventing damage at the source in the event of a leak. Given that recent personal information leakage incidents often occur in security blind spots such as unencrypted logs, long-term idle data, or key management negligence, data center security policies have become crucial. D.AMO onOS v5.0 can encrypt all data, including idle data, thereby eliminating vulnerabilities that attackers could exploit. Furthermore, it encrypts all log data, including decryption records, ensuring that even if data is leaked, attackers cannot obtain plaintext. The product ensures encryption performance close to plaintext in large network file system environments like NFS or Samba, while also improving system availability. The platform has integrated NIST standard Post-Quantum Cryptography (PQC) and Korea Post-Quantum Cryptography (KpqC) algorithms, preparing for the era of quantum computing.",
